But note: should we allow defining a word whose body references another user word defined later? Not in the tests. Standard Forth errors. Error at definition time.

Hmm, but actually there's a subtle point: should the name be resolved case-insensitively? Yes, lowercase everything.

Execution: for each line, tokenize; if the first token is `:` handle as definition; otherwise execute each token: number → push; word → look up defs; if found execute the ops (inlined); if not found error "undefined operation".

Since builtins and user words are all `[]op` in the same map, execution of a user word = iterate its ops.

